  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 384 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
